> db/migrations/20260917101500_add_orders_index.sql

  x error MR101 Index creation blocks writes on "orders"

     ,- db/migrations/20260917101500_add_orders_index.sql:2:1
   1 | BEGIN;
   2 | CREATE INDEX idx_orders_created_at ON orders (created_at);
     | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
     |
     |- lock    SHARE on orders - blocks INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
     |- why     Postgres holds this lock until the whole index is built. INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE
     |          on the table wait for the entire build.
     `- fix     Build the index concurrently, outside a transaction:

                CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_orders_created_at ON orders (created_at);

> db/migrations/20260917101600_add_orders_user_fk.sql

  x error MR104 Foreign key blocks writes on "orders" and "users"

     ,- db/migrations/20260917101600_add_orders_user_fk.sql:1:24
   1 | ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_user_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES use...
     |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^...
     |
     |- lock    SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE on orders, users - blocks INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
     |- why     Postgres checks every existing row of orders against users while it holds locks on
     |          both tables. INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE on either table wait until the check
     |          finishes.
     `- fix     Add the constraint as NOT VALID, then validate it in a separate transaction:

                1  Add the constraint without checking existing rows
                   ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_user_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users (id) NOT VALID;

                2  Validate it in a separate migration
                   ALTER TABLE orders VALIDATE CONSTRAINT orders_user_id_fkey;

> db/migrations/20260917101700_widen_user_name.sql

  ! warning MR201 Changing the type of "users.name" may rewrite the table

     ,- db/migrations/20260917101700_widen_user_name.sql:1:1
   1 | ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN name TYPE varchar(255);
     | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
     |
     |- lock    ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on users - blocks reads and writes - rewrites the table
     |- why     Some changes to this type only update the catalog, such as varchar to text or a
     |          longer varchar limit. Other changes rewrite every row of users under an ACCESS
     |          EXCLUSIVE lock. migrail can't see the current column type in this migration.
     `- fix     Change the type with expand and contract instead of rewriting the table in place:

                1  Add name_new with the new type
                   ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN name_new varchar(255);

                2  Write to both columns and backfill name_new in batches

                3  Read from name_new, then drop name and rename name_new

> db/migrations/20260917102000_rename_user_email.sql

  x error MR302 Renaming column "users.email" breaks running code

     ,- db/migrations/20260917102000_rename_user_email.sql:1:33
   1 | ALTER TABLE users RENAME COLUMN email TO email_address;
     |                                 ^^^^^
     |
     |- lock    ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on users - blocks reads and writes
     |- why     During a rolling deploy, instances running the previous release still query "email".
     |          Those queries fail as soon as this migration runs.
     `- fix     Rename in three deploys with expand and contract:
                1  Add email_address, write to both columns and backfill it
                2  Read from email_address and stop writing email
                3  Drop email

